# Rolls-Royce Silver Spirit four-door saloon, 1980-1998.
#
# The Silver Spirit (and its long-wheelbase Spur): 5,278 mm long, 1,887 mm wide,
# 1,486 mm high, 3,061 mm wheelbase; 6.75-litre V8, the last of the Crewe
# coach-built generation. Silver Spirit II from 1989. About 8,000 Spirits and
# Spurs built.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Silver_Spirit
#
# Colours: Black, Silver Sand, Royal Blue and Burgundy are documented
# Rolls-Royce finishes of the period.
#
# Weight: 15 in total (black 5, silver 4, blue 3, burgundy 3), the rarest class-4
# model of its decade.
#
# Speed 210 km/h; comfort 150/405 (line). Class 4.
# Dates: 1980-1998 with a road tail to about 2012.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rolls-royce-silver-spirit.blend. References:
# citycars/references/rolls-royce-silver-spirit/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia
# Commons.

obj=citycar
